# --- Deny ALL root-level dotfiles and dot-directories -------------------------
# Deliberately a denylist-of-last-resort inverted into an allowlist: enumerating
# individual dot-dirs is fragile, and anything missed is silently baked into a
# customer-facing image. This has already bitten us — local ClickHouse data
# (.clickhouse/, ~1.7 GB of real analytics), .ruby-lsp/ and .claude/ all leaked
# in that way. Deny everything, re-admit only what the build genuinely needs.
.*
!.ruby-version

# Belt-and-braces: these must never ship even if the rule above changes.
.env
.env.*
.kamal/
.clickhouse/
config/master.key
config/credentials.yml.enc

# Logs, caches and local ActiveStorage blobs. The directories themselves still
# exist in the image — Rails recreates them during assets:precompile in the
# builder stage — so only their contents are dropped.
log/*
tmp/*
storage/*
node_modules/

# Test/Dev
spec/
test/
ee/test/
coverage/
.rspec

# Docs ship alongside the image, not inside it
docs/

# Deploy tooling. config/deploy.yml and these Dockerfiles are symlinks into a
# developer checkout, so they land in the image as dangling links exposing local
# paths; the real deploy.yml would expose production host IPs and topology.
config/deploy.yml
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.test
Dockerfile.preview
Dockerfile.development
Dockerfile.production
docker-compose.yml
Procfile*
run_*.sh

# MaxMind GeoLite2 is licensed to us, not to our customers — redistributing it
# inside a shipped image would breach the EULA. Self-hosted deployments supply
# their own database and point GEOIP_DB_PATH at it. Geo features degrade
# gracefully when it is absent (see config/initializers/geoip.rb).
db/*.mmdb

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/

# OS
.DS_Store

# Private keys must never ride into an image
resources/*.p8
**/*.p8
